request.description:
Validates each row independently and **always returns 200**, even when some rows fail. Max 5000 rows.

The sample body is deliberately mixed: rows 1 and 2 succeed, row 3 fails on three fields at once, row 4 collides with row 1 from the same batch.

```json
{
  "added": [ { "id": 5, "code": "BULK-001", ... } ],
  "failed": [
    {
      "row": { "code": "BULK-003", "name": "", ... },
      "errors": {
        "name": "Material name is required",
        "categoryId": "Selected category does not exist",
        "uom": "Unrecognized unit of measure"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Every problem is reported at once rather than one at a time. The code collides with the seeded `MAT-001-1-001` (compared case-insensitively).

Expected:
```json
{
  "errors": {
    "code": "This item code already exists",
    "name": "Material name is required",
    "categoryId": "Selected category does not exist",
    "uom": "Unrecognized unit of measure"
  }
}
```
